  "architecture": {
    "type": "architecture",
    "title": "How a request reaches the agent",
    "source": "docs/architecture.md, \"The shape\"",
    "summary": "Requests travel from the browser over HTTPS through the ALB to the cimip service. The service writes to Aurora PostgreSQL, puts sealed segments in S3, calls Bedrock for the scribe and has ECS start one agent sandbox per incident. It streams HTTP + SSE to the sandbox, which calls Bedrock for inference, sends its logs to CloudWatch and runs approved tools against production.",
